WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:08.207
“abcde” and “ace” share letters in order, but which run is longest?

00:08.207 --> 00:14.700
Listing every subsequence of each word explodes fast.

00:15.000 --> 00:18.788
Build a table instead.

00:18.788 --> 00:31.700
Each cell answers a smaller question: how much do these two prefixes share?

00:32.000 --> 00:35.504
Fill it corner to corner.

00:35.504 --> 00:42.934
‘c’ meets ‘c’, so take the diagonal 1 and add one: 2.

00:42.934 --> 00:47.700
A miss carries the best neighbour.

00:48.000 --> 00:51.951
The corner reads 3: “ace”.

00:51.951 --> 00:57.573
One pass over the table, O(m·n) time.

00:57.573 --> 00:59.700
That’s 2-D DP.

